+# Mandatory regression requirements after the experimental v1 freeze
+
+Permanent requirement: **A_out ⊆ A_in** for each individual transformation at
+its effective creation point, with legitimate provenance, effective restrictions,
+independent grants and the class's defined delegation permissions accounted for.
+Every future class must demonstrate this through reproducible tests.
+
+Do not compare an independent historical capability against its source's later
+reduced state. Do not call two descriptor numbers independent. Do not reconstruct
+rights from UID 0 or an identity-only snapshot. Shared-state attenuation, task
+credential COW, private clone ownership and explicit global revocation are
+separate contracts. Existing LSM/DAC/namespace/filesystem/device restrictions
+remain applicable according to their documented composition boundary.
+
+## Before any candidate qualification
+
+1. Verify the frozen baseline manifest and reconstruct it independently. Record
+   candidate base, complete tracked/untracked source delta and exact source/code
+   hashes. Preserve baseline artifacts; never update the baseline version in place.
+2. Classify each affected transformation: actual input/holder, grant provenance,
+   output object, aliasing/independence, restrictions, lifetime and linearization.
+   Identify absent, unhandled and claimed-but-unimplemented operations explicitly.
+3. Declare affected configs/workloads from source changes, not from convenient
+   earlier PASS totals. Build the actual candidate source including untracked
+   files. Retain full .config, toolchain, UAPI headers, binaries and QEMU commands.
+4. Keep native controls, custom Authority assertions, LSM denials, fixture setup,
+   FAIL/SKIP/BROKEN/BLOCKED and executable/group/assertion counts separate.
+5. Do not silently weaken assertions/LSM rules or rebase saved credentials to
+   obtain green results. Explain fixture failures and retain failed runs.
+
+## Minimum change-impact matrix
+
+| Change surface | Required retained/new checks |
+|---|---|
+| Core classification/state/registry | Core KUnit, unhandled/implemented/unimplemented/unknown cases, immutable handled-state reductions; old filesystem and temporal suites |
+| Filesystem evaluator/scope/DAC/VFS | authority_test, qualification_test, meaningful ramfs variant, idmapped_test, callback_test, acquisition/handle tests where path affected; matched native/pristine comparisons and relevant LTP subset |
+| FD clone/restrict/description lifetime | zero/R/RW maximum intersection, before/after/concurrent reduction, independent retention/re-delegation, shared dup/SCM/fork/fixed slots, offset/mode/flags, mmap/mprotect/transfers, close/reuse; temporal_test and relevant Landlock regressions |
+| Credentials/fork/exec | objective versus subjective issuer state, COW snapshots, inherited established handles, confined exec persistence, same UID with different Authority, no source-identity-only restoration; temporal and LSM adoption tests |
+| Delegation/attenuation | actual legitimate source, transfer/recipient restrictions, independent versus shared state and explicitly authorized additional grants; no implicit retroactive revocation; existing temporal/FD coverage plus candidate boundary tests |
+| LSM/context/cache hooks | focused Landlock/SELinux/AppArmor with allowed controls and independent denials, saved optional/cache constraints, enforcing selected stacks, current adoption veto; matching policy ABI and failed-fixture retention |
+| Async execution/ring/personality | registration before/after reduction, default issuer versus explicit context, in-flight/unregister/teardown, inherited/shared ring namespace, EBUSY/ordering, LSM veto; test any newly claimed async mode separately |
+| User/mount/other namespaces | stable object identity, idmaps, cross-mount/namespace errors, constructor privilege and DAC/ACL/LSM checks; namespace combinations must not be inferred passing |
+| Concurrency/object ownership | bounded races with defined legal outcomes, completed-reduction ordering, UAF/double-free/reference lifetime; appropriate KASAN/lockdep/strict KCSAN differential controls and reviewed reports |
+| UAPI/build/config compatibility | native and IA32 where supported, malformed/version/size/unknown bits, correct errors/failure atomicity, supported config builds and Linux compatibility; no fictitious feature-off result |
+| New resource class | typed context/state/evaluator and lifecycle checks for all above applicable surfaces; reproducible class-specific provenance, alias/independence, delegation, inheritance, effective restrictions and fail-closed behavior |
+
+Reuse tools/testing/selftests/authority/ and run-qemu.sh; existing specialized LSM,
+XFS, idmap and acquisition fixture recipes are in the frozen evidence. Do not
+create a parallel general runner, audit store or lifecycle subsystem merely
+because a new class is being considered. Extend the owning tests narrowly.
+
+At minimum no unauthorized amplification, no restoration from a locally reduced
+input, correct temporal independence, correct alias propagation, no unintended
+native Linux/LSM regression, and no unexplained applicable lifetime/concurrency
+defect may remain for a claimed feature. New explicit global revocation would
+require a separate defined contract and tests; the current absent API remains
+SKIP/unimplemented, not a preexisting mechanism to reuse by assumption.
+
+## Requalification and decisions
+
+Source equality can establish applicability of retained historical evidence;
+it does not convert it into a newly executed run. No production change requires
+unrelated expensive suites to be repeated without cause. A relevant change must
+rerun its affected suites/instrumentation, and a new unknown source state cannot
+inherit PASS solely from a similar branch name.
+
+Keep the existing eight independent gates and their accepted boundaries. New
+findings need memory/stack/synchronization/source/config/workload analysis, not
+warning-string dismissal. Independent upstream classification is attribution,
+not a claim of harmlessness or sanitizer-clean Linux. Execution restrictions
+remain BLOCKED/not executed, never worked around. No host deployment or reboot
+is needed. Assign a new candidate version/decision; do not mutate the frozen
+experimental v1 reference or manufacture GO from high pass counts.
