+# Targeted Authority / Landlock compatibility audit
+
+## Verdict and scope
+
+**COMPATIBLE_WITH_DOCUMENTED_LIMITATIONS after the cached-permission fix.**
+This is not a production qualification of Filesystem Authority v1. The original
+image had a real clone-specific Landlock permission-amplification defect, but
+it was **not** the READ behavior flagged by the previous qualification test.
+The complete evidence is `/tmp/authority-landlock-audit/REPORT.md`; preserve that
+directory durably before loss of temporary storage.
+
+Baseline is HEAD `e767a4ea70a3992c37ed604157d32f0dfbf9b1e3` plus the preserved
+worktree in `/tmp/authority-v1/source-final.tar` (SHA-256
+`710f021dd578b3e6da29e2677d851be1365877f95d4e4e107bc5a0265fa8d384`).
+No existing class, right, filesystem UAPI or selective/sealed transition changed.
+
+## The old failure was a test-contract error
+
+Linux/Landlock deliberately keep permissions associated with an already opened
+file. dup/F_DUPFD/fork/exec/SCM_RIGHTS retain that open file description and its
+security state. A fresh pathname or procfs reopen is different and is checked
+again. See Documentation/userspace-api/landlock.rst, “Rights associated with
+file descriptors”. Landlock does not register a file_permission hook to revoke
+READ/WRITE each time the current thread uses an older FD.
+
+F_CLONEFD_CAP is neither dup nor a fresh pathname acquisition. It derives an
+independent description from a pinned source path; its Authority bitmap is
+`source & request & destination_mode`. It retains source->f_cred, allocating a
+fresh LSM security blob and running normal inode/open/post-open hooks. This is
+intentional bearer derivation; it does not install the saved credentials in the
+caller or change the caller's Authority/Landlock domain.
+
+Therefore the old assertion “fresh path READ is denied, so cloning an existing
+pre-Landlock READ FD must also be denied” was **TEST_CONTRACT_ERROR**. Its
+corrected regression requires a readable READ-only clone, denied WRITE, and
+continued fresh-path denial. It passes on both the original and fixed kernel.
+The minimal reproducer contains no Authority-domain setup at all; the same
+behavior occurs with the Core unhandled.
+
+## The distinct implementation defect
+
+Landlock caches optional TRUNCATE/IOCTL_DEV access in each file's
+`landlock_file_security.allowed_access`. Clone used to recompute that state
+under saved opener credentials without comparing it to the source cache.
+
+The regression closes the fixture's pre-Landlock data FD, installs a policy
+allowing READ/WRITE in a and b but TRUNCATE only in b, then opens a/file.
+Source ftruncate is denied. A later layer denies all new data opens. An
+external helper (forked before Landlock, without a data FD) moves a/file into b.
+Source and dup still cannot truncate; a fresh open is denied. The old clone
+nevertheless acquired TRUNCATE and shortened the object to zero. Its READ/WRITE
+bitmap stayed 3, so an Authority-bitmap-only test would miss this defect.
+
+**IMPLEMENTATION_DEFECT:** losing a stored Landlock denial during capability
+derivation, not standard Linux non-retroactivity. The external helper supplies
+a namespace move, not a replacement FD or a new task policy grant.
+
+The focused fix adds a deny-only LSM `file_clone(source, destination)` check
+after existing open/post-open checks and before FD publication. Landlock
+rejects (`EACCES`) if recomputed optional rights exceed the source cache. It
+does not rebase credentials, copy opaque LSM blobs, modify cached audit masks,
+revoke old FDs, or weaken any existing hook. The clone is conservatively
+rejected rather than trying to manufacture partially intersected opaque LSM
+state. Rejection unwinds through the existing fput/bitmap cleanup path.
+
+## Differential results
+
+Counts are grouped kselftests, not individual syscalls. Raw `OBS` records retain
+return values and errno, source/clone rights, offset behavior and object size.
+
+| Configuration | Targeted groups PASS/FAIL/SKIP |
+|---|---:|
+| A: pristine HEAD, Landlock enabled, no custom API | 4/0/3 |
+| B-unhandled: fixed modified kernel, no task Authority domain | 6/0/1 |
+| C: fixed modified kernel, Authority domain enabled, CONFIG_SECURITY_LANDLOCK=n | 5/0/2 |
+| C-unhandled: same C image, no domain | 4/0/3 |
+| D before fix: Authority and Landlock enabled | 6/1/0 |
+| D after fix: Authority and Landlock enabled | 7/0/0 |
+
+**Requested fully Authority-disabled modified build B is BLOCKED:** no such
+Kconfig/runtime switch exists. B-unhandled leaves the credential domain absent,
+but the FD API is still compiled. It must not be called feature-off. No switch
+was invented for this audit. KUNIT=n also is not Authority-off.
+
+On the fixed regular and KASAN/lockdep images, complete executed userspace
+regressions each report **533 PASS / 0 FAIL / 14 SKIP**, including the original
+13, qualification 22, targeted 7, ramfs variant, four upstream openat2 suites,
+and upstream Landlock base/fs tests. Core checks separately pass **10/10** on
+both images. Static compat32 authority suites pass **42/0/0**. Skips are ramfs
+ACL (1), upstream overlayfs (3), hostfs (5), tracefs (5). No KASAN/lockdep warning
+was observed; strict KCSAN was not rerun in this focused audit.
+
+## Classification and limitations
+
+* **EXPECTED_LINUX_BEHAVIOR:** old FD/dup/SCM/fork/exec access persists; source
+  ftruncate and device ioctl keep their open-time Landlock properties; fresh
+  path/proc reopen can still fail; denied directory listing is not universal
+  traversal/metadata confinement.
+* **EXPECTED_AUTHORITY_BEHAVIOR:** independent clone offset and saved opener;
+  monotonic bit attenuation; managed regular-file ioctl fails EOPNOTSUPP;
+  device FD clone unsupported; changed UID/FSUID can use a delegated object
+  without gaining fresh path access. Foreign-source and foreign-clone
+  AT_EMPTY_PATH publication both retain Linux's ENOENT credential gate.
+* **TEST_CONTRACT_ERROR:** treating preexisting bearer READ as a fresh path
+  grant merely because clone allocates a new struct file.
+* **IMPLEMENTATION_DEFECT, fixed:** source optional-permission cache was not
+  a ceiling on recomputed clone state after a move. New regression verifies
+  EACCES and unchanged object size/source denial.
+* **POLICY_AMBIGUITY / UNQUALIFIED:** stronger process-wide FD revocation,
+  caller-credential rebasing, other LSMs' cached restrictions, enforcing
+  SELinux/AppArmor stacking, device cloning, and full feature-off comparison.
+  No such additional policy is silently chosen here. Clone can still fail
+  when ordinary LSM recomputation denies it; it is not promised dup's exact
+  success behavior across path/policy changes. Clone-guard rejection is not
+  integrated into a new Landlock audit-request type; kprobes observe it.
+
+Entry/return kprobes observe file_open, file_permission, file_post_open,
+file_truncate, the Landlock callbacks, and the new file_clone guard without
+replacing their decisions. The fixed moved-object case runs open/post-open,
+then file_clone returns -EACCES before publication. The source and clone have
+independent security blobs/lifetimes; old descriptions are not overwritten.
+The existing whole-kernel NO-GO and its unrelated regression/integration/
+concurrency blockers are not lifted by this targeted verdict.
