+# Qualification status, boundaries, and next work
+
+This status records what can be defended, not what the prototype hopes eventually to do. Four labels matter throughout:
+
+* **CURRENT SOURCE** — checked in the present worktree during this documentation task.
+* **HISTORICAL RUNTIME-REPORTED** — the previous isolated-QEMU run reported the result in the surviving conversation summary, but the original `/tmp` test sources/logs were lost after reboot. These results are not independently rerun in this documentation task.
+* **CURRENT RUNTIME-REPORTED** — a current isolated-QEMU run of the exact built image produced retained temporary logs and machine-readable markers; the harness/artifacts are not repository tests.
+* **SOURCE-REVIEWED** — source flow was inspected, but no corresponding runtime proof is retained.
+
+Do not silently upgrade historical or partial evidence into a universal claim. The original reports `/tmp/authority-cve-eval/report.md`, `/tmp/authority-dac-audit/report.md`, and `/tmp/authority-create-minting/report.md` are absent. The recovery notes live in `../authority-prototype/`.
+
+## 1. Qualification vocabulary
+
+| Label | Meaning |
+|---|---|
+| **QUALIFIED (bounded)** | Relevant path was exercised on the exact built kernel in an isolated runtime with synthetic fixtures. This covers only stated configurations/paths; it is not a proof for all filesystems or races. |
+| **PARTIALLY QUALIFIED** | Some important path variants were tested, but meaningful operations/configurations remain outside evidence. |
+| **SOURCE-REVIEWED** | Code path/order was inspected without matching runtime evidence. |
+| **UNQUALIFIED** | No defensible test/source basis for a behavior claim. |
+| **FAILED** | A stated intended invariant was tested and violated. Keep the negative result visible. |
+| **OUT_OF_MODEL** | Mechanism is outside the stated filesystem-authority trust boundary (e.g. arbitrary kernel compromise). |
+| **BLOCKED** | Meaningful qualification depends on an unavailable precondition, policy, filesystem, or safe test setup. |
+
+“Zero test failures” is a test result, not a security proof and not evidence for untested entry points.
+
+## 2. Current source inventory and explicit coverage limits
+
+`kernel/authority.c` and `include/linux/authority.h` hold credential-associated class state. The minimal internal Authority Core dispatches typed class-local requests and reports UNHANDLED, HANDLED+IMPLEMENTED, or HANDLED+UNIMPLEMENTED; filesystem authorization and regular-open DAC composition remain distributed mainly in `fs/namei.c`, with open/truncate logic in `fs/open.c`. File-description capability handling is in `fs/file_capability.c`, `fs/read_write.c`, `fs/open.c`, `fs/ioctl.c`, and `mm/mmap.c`. Control ABI remains the existing PoC `prctl` in `kernel/sys.c` / `include/uapi/linux/prctl.h`; FD ABI remains the existing PoC `fcntl` commands in `include/uapi/linux/fcntl.h`.
+
+**CURRENT SOURCE:** `PR_CAPAUTH_CONFINE` can mark only `CREATE_FILE`, `READ_FILE`, `WRITE_FILE`, `DELETE_FILE`, `RENAME`, and `LINK` as handled. `TRAVERSE` exists as an additive/path permission right but cannot be made mandatory by this ABI. DAC override itself is not a handled right; entry rejects the legacy global override. Thus do not state that current confinement covers every right in the enum or all pathname reachability.
+
+**CURRENT SOURCE:** `PR_CAPAUTH_ADD_FS_SCOPE` requires `CAP_SYS_ADMIN`; `AUTH_SYSTEM` also requires it. The PoC does not yet expose the general unprivileged launcher/broker API implied by the long-term use case. Any claimed deployment flow must account for a privileged authority-construction step.
+
+## 3. Runtime-reported qualification matrix
+
+The previous report recorded a full external Debian Trixie build (GCC 14.2.0, GNU ld 2.44) and booted the produced image only in isolated QEMU/KVM with synthetic fixtures. The final recorded `bzImage` SHA-256 was `c0694f3a9a7d70cff6676fb2adafe725e3a7872a67c0b6fe80e3870c7b56d569`; config SHA-256 was `5ab2b496a41786dd90a780c5a063aa93e785351484158d29d28b422f9decd3ea`. Build/runtime artifacts and logs were in `/tmp` and are no longer present. Hashes are historical identifiers, not proof the artifacts can be reproduced today.
+
+| Area | Status | Retained result / limit |
+|---|---|---|
+| Identity separate from authority | **HISTORICAL RUNTIME-REPORTED** | Early `AUTH_SYSTEM` proof reportedly retained ordinary user UID/GID and zero Linux capabilities while selected operations succeeded; created objects kept ordinary ownership. Broad mode is PoC scaffolding. Original harness lost. |
+| Variable-width rights | **PARTIALLY QUALIFIED** | Bit-80 sentinel was used to test storage/control parsing above 64 bits; not a general extensible multi-class ABI proof. Unknown set bits fail closed in current confine parser; zero extension bytes accepted. |
+| Object-backed scopes | **HISTORICAL RUNTIME-REPORTED** | Rename/replacement, symlink spelling, and bind-alias behaviors were tested in synthetic guests. Exact matrix/logs lost; unusual mounts/filesystems/races remain unqualified. Current source matches same mount+dentry ancestry for most rights and exact identity for DELETE/RENAME. |
+| `CREATE_FILE` separation | **HISTORICAL RUNTIME-REPORTED** | CREATE-only did not imply existing READ/WRITE, mkdir, delete, or rename in prior tests. This is not universal CREATE-path coverage. |
+| Bounded `TRAVERSE` | **PARTIALLY QUALIFIED** | Historical bounded BENEATH/IN_ROOT tests reportedly rejected `..`, symlink escape, wrong-parent, and alias cases. Current confine ABI cannot mark TRAVERSE mandatory; lookup fast paths / ambient path visibility are not a complete boundary. |
+| Existing-file READ/WRITE opens and DAC provider | **CURRENT RUNTIME-REPORTED; QUALIFIED (bounded)** | Exact integration image: 47 focused cases, zero failures. Includes mode/group and FSUID/FSGID, ACL and supplementary groups, DAC capabilities/mandatory ceiling, O_RDWR composition, O_TRUNC and path `truncate()`, path/proc reopen, hard-link/symlink/renamed-scope/bind aliases, mmap/mprotect FD ceilings, sendfile/splice/copy_file_range FD-capability checks, and CREATE/O_TMPFILE/LINK/DELETE/RENAME regressions. Generic DAC is reused, not duplicated. Callback filesystems, idmapped mounts, enforcing LSM, races, and alternate fresh-open paths remain unqualified; see §7. |
+| FD restriction/derivation | **PARTIALLY QUALIFIED** | GET/restrict/clone, subset behavior, dup family sharing, fork/exec, SCM_RIGHTS, read/write, truncate/fallocate, mmap/mprotect, and sendfile/splice/copy_file_range checks tested on supported simple regular-file filesystems. The file-capability code supports regular rootfs/ramfs/tmpfs inodes except `IS_ANON_FILE()` and path/backing FDs; this includes memfd shmem inodes, whose unscoped creation/data access remains outside path confinement. Existing mappings remain non-revocable. |
+| FD persistence after scope drop | **QUALIFIED (bounded)** | Retained tests showed established FD use persists after pathname scopes drop. This is an intentional bearer-capability property, not a bypass claim. Existing mappings/imported writable FDs are not revoked. |
+| Procfs reopen from attenuated FD | **FAILED for additive model; later bounded fix reported** | Initially a READ-only clone's direct write failed but a fresh `/proc/self/fd/N` O_WRONLY open succeeded through ambient DAC. Mandatory fresh-open checks later denied tested proc reopen cases. The additional same-UID `/proc/<pid>/fd/N` test passed the ptrace access precondition but was denied by the receiver's handled semantic scope. Other import/reopen routes remain. |
+| Mandatory confinement for handled rights | **QUALIFIED (bounded)** | Previous rootfs/tmpfs synthetic suites reported that UID DAC and `CAP_DAC_OVERRIDE` did not exceed handled READ/WRITE/CREATE/DELETE/RENAME scopes; positive semantic grants worked; unknown handled bits failed closed; fork/exec/setid/filecap transitions were exercised. Follow-up tests cover selected exceptional file-description routes only. Anonymous memfd/SysV shared-memory storage is explicitly outside this path-authority result. |
+| CREATE initial FD rights | **QUALIFIED (bounded)** | Final reported 4-way READ/WRITE mask matrix for named `O_CREAT`, `open/openat/openat2/creat`, `O_TMPFILE`, existing `O_CREAT`, `O_EXCL`, new/existing `O_TRUNC`, FD bits vs `F_GETFL`, descriptor persistence, restrictions, and read-only tmpfs. `CREATE_MINTING_FAILURES=0`. `dentry_create()` O_TRUNC access adjustment was source-reviewed, not runtime-tested. See [create report](../authority-prototype/create-file-authority.rst). |
+| DELETE | **PARTIALLY QUALIFIED** | Direct-child non-directory unlink API exercised; exact-parent and separation from data rights reported. `rmdir`, all unbounded/alternate delete callers, special filesystems and races are not complete. |
+| RENAME | **PARTIALLY QUALIFIED** | Isolated tests reported zero failures for direct-child regular files, exact both-parent semantics, flags zero, and existing FD behavior. The bounded capability API rejects directory/nonzero-flag cases; ordinary `renameat2` flows have separate parent-aware VFS checks but directory/exchange/nonzero flags were not runtime-qualified. Leases/delegations/race behavior is not complete. |
