+**CURRENT RUNTIME-REPORTED:** a clean external build in `/tmp/authority-dac-integration/build` (Debian Trixie, Linux `7.3.0-rc5`, GCC 14.2.0, GNU ld 2.44) produced the exact image booted under isolated QEMU/KVM. The final harness reported `DAC_INTEGRATION_CASES=47`, `DAC_INTEGRATION_FAILURES=0`, `DAC_INTEGRATION_EXIT=0`, then normal power down. It also reported CREATE subset 3/0, LINK subset 4/0, DELETE subset 2/0, RENAME subset 2/0, focused confinement 34/0, FD capability 6/0, and aggregate DAC-provider failures 0. Cases include mode/group, FSUID/FSGID, ACL and supplementary groups, DAC-capability ceilings, O_RDWR, O_TRUNC, explicit `truncate(path)` WRITE grant and mandatory denial, ftruncate distinction, path/proc reopen, hard-link/symlink/renamed-scope/bind aliases, CREATE/O_TMPFILE/LINK/DELETE/RENAME regressions, EROFS, shared mmap/mprotect attenuation, fallocate, FD attenuation/delegation, and FD-capability-gated `sendfile`, `splice`, and `copy_file_range`.
