+Exact integration evidence: `bzImage` SHA-256 `38df41ec4d909994109a6dc8f8154e6e42c9fdd65ab4109265bed9b24a1e6f79`; config SHA-256 `d6fe1c4979b1d630b9212cfe11a36231de7117f8cd55e49af19c8ac18e5044c2`; rootfs cpio SHA-256 `0df3b2dbf1faa60e8277f760d16055cdd5ce8723eef87a762edcaa98f34a52e1`; harness source SHA-256 `781330755e37a9a355ae9c6a0c8182ac7d87ddc250a61b27f4d3d39ab6ff57c8`; static test binary SHA-256 `18852b4f13c7fc675cef6eaef0cea57470ff6aa0a45d374120601eee99177ba9`. The FD-path test included a `F_SETFL(O_RDWR|O_APPEND)` attempt followed by a denied READ operation, confirming attenuation was not restored. XFS was configured as a module and compiled; the guest suite did not load XFS or exercise `open_by_handle`.
