+The source audit found ordinary `open/openat/openat2`, io_uring openat/openat2, and procfs FD reopen converge on the normal open path. `rw_verify_area()` checks LSM file permission and managed FD READ/WRITE rights; representative FD I/O and mmap tests remain bounded to the existing integration harness. `F_SETFL` cannot change `f_mode`/`O_ACCMODE` or restore an attenuated FD right. XFS `open_by_handle` bypasses `may_open()` and generic DAC, but checks the handled semantic READ/WRITE ceiling and retains `CAP_SYS_ADMIN`; generic `open_by_handle_at()` uses handle resolution and then VFS open checks. Both were runtime-tested on a synthetic XFS v5 fixture in the follow-up. Fanotify event-FD creation bypassed `may_open()` and was found to deliver a readable FD despite a denied fresh open; `create_fd()` now checks the handled regular-file ceiling, and the retest returned `-EACCES` in `FAN_REPORT_FD_ERROR`. Overlayfs `ovl_permission()` remains a custom callback whose failures are not overridden. Callback filesystems remain unqualified.
