+  pre-existing pair. General benignness/compiler behavior is not asserted.
+* Serial, 7.266288 s: CPU0 PID1 `console_on_rootfs` startup assigns the software
+  `uart_8250_port.ier` shadow outside port.lock after IRQ setup; CPU3 IRQ reads
+  its THRI bit under port.lock. The tty mutex is not that IRQ lock. Q35 ttyS0
+  is the native 16550A at 0x3f8/IRQ4. This is not MMIO false sharing. The writer
+  ancestry does include modified VFS code, which can shift timing/layout; that
+  connection was examined, not denied. The console is S_IFCHR, unsupported for
+  managed regular-file capabilities, boot Authority=NULL and file-cap field
+  initialization is in separate file memory. No IER/IRQ/port-lock/layout/lifetime
+  change is made by Authority. The native startup/IRQ pair is reachable unchanged
+  in pristine. No driver safety claim or silencing fix follows.
